class:: TempoStability
summary:: Confidence-weighted tempo stability
categories:: UGens>Analysis>Rhythm
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Onsets2, Classes/BeatTrack3

description::
Computes the weighted standard deviation of log2(BPM) over a trailing control-rate window, then exp(-12*deviation). Fewer than two accepted observations yields zero; perfectly steady accepted tempo yields one.

This is an independent implementation of the statistical definition above. Output updates at the server control rate; beat boundaries are quantized to a control block. Silence produces zero level/density or missing tempo evidence. No corpus-level accuracy is implied.

classmethods::
method:: kr
argument:: bpm
Control-rate tempo in BPM; nonpositive and nonfinite values are rejected as missing evidence.

argument:: confidence
Control-rate evidence weight, normally 0–1, default 1.

argument:: windowTime
Trailing history in seconds. Rhythm analysis accepts 0.5–16, default 6; onset/tempo statistics accept 0.05–60, default 4.

argument:: minConfidence
Minimum accepted confidence, default 0.1.

returns::
One stability score from 0 to 1.

examples::
TempoStability computes the confidence-weighted standard deviation of tempo over a rolling control window, outputting a normalized score ($1.0$ for rock-solid mechanical timing, decaying toward $0.0$ during tempo drifts and rubato). In this example, it controls feedback on a stereo flanger: steady tempos produce resonant metallic comb tones, while tempo fluctuations cleanly damp the feedback. An interactive code::MIR2GUI.scope:: plots the real-time stability score.
code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var path = MIR2GUI.soundPath("drums.wav");
    ~mir2Buffer = if(path.notNil) { Buffer.read(s, path) } { nil };
    ~mir2Bus = Bus.control(s, 1);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) {
            PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1)
        } {
            // Synthetic drum fallback
            var trig = Impulse.kr(2);
            var kick = SinOsc.ar(EnvGen.ar(Env([120, 45], [0.08], \exp), trig)) * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.3), trig);
            var snare = WhiteNoise.ar * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.005, 0.15), Impulse.kr(2, 0.5));
            (kick + snare) * 0.5
        };
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);

        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, 0.25);
        var onset = Onsets2.kr(chain, threshold: 0.15, fftSize: 1024, hop: 0.25);
        var tempo = Tempo.kr(onset[1], tempoSmooth: 0.2);
        var stable = TempoStability.kr(tempo[0], tempo[1], windowTime: 3.0);
        var stableSmooth = stable.lag(0.04);

        // Flanger feedback gated by tempo stability
        var flangerMod = SinOsc.kr(0.4, [0, pi/2], 0.002, 0.005);
        var flanger = CombC.ar(source, 0.02, flangerMod, stableSmooth.linlin(0, 1, 0.1, 0.8)) * 0.3;
        var sound = (source * 0.25 ! 2) + flanger;

        if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { Out.kr(~mir2Bus, stable) };
        sound * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.2)
    }.play;

    ~mir2GUI = MIR2GUI.scope("Tempo Stability", ~mir2Bus, 0.0, 1.0);
});
)
::
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
if(~mir2GUI.notNil) { ~mir2GUI.close };
if(~mir2Bus.notNil) { ~mir2Bus.free };
if(~mir2Buffer.notNil) { ~mir2Buffer.free };
)
::

